---
const items = [
  {
    title: "Overall safety",
    body: "Guangxi is well-policed and tourist-friendly. Guilin, Yangshuo and Nanning are among the safest places in China for travelers, including solo women. Violent crime against visitors is rare.",
  },
  {
    title: "Common tourist traps",
    body: "Watch for overcharging at stalls near Li River piers and West Street, and for unlicensed taxis outside stations. Use Didi or licensed cabs, agree raft and driver prices in advance, and check the menu before ordering.",
  },
  {
    title: "Health and food",
    body: "Stick to busy stalls and bottled or boiled water. Luosifen and street food are generally safe when freshly cooked. Carry a basic medical kit; larger cities have international-standard hospitals, but rural Hechi and Longji have limited clinics.",
  },
  {
    title: "Weather and terrain",
    body: "Summer heat and humidity peak from June to August, and the Li River and Yulong River can swell after heavy rain. Karst paths and Longji's stairs are steep and can be slippery when wet; wear grippy shoes.",
  },
  {
    title: "Border areas",
    body: "The Vietnam border near Detian and Dongxing is heavily monitored. Stay within marked tourist zones, keep your passport handy, and never attempt to cross informally, which requires a separate Vietnamese visa.",
  },
];
---
<section id="safety" class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 pb-1">
          Is Guangxi safe?
        </h2>
        <p class="text-stone-500 text-lg mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          Short answer: yes. Guangxi is one of China's easier, safer regions for foreign travelers. A few honest caveats so nothing catches you off guard.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        {items.map((it) => (
          <div class="flex gap-6 py-6 border-t border-stone-200 last:border-b">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-36">
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-stone-900">{it.title}</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">{it.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
